{
  "note": [
    "The labelled commands `laya_advisor.py --fit` refits its temperatures on, and the whole basis",
    "for the numbers in TEMPERATURES. laya's card says the checkpoint ships over-confident and that",
    "one temperature per (question type, option count) has to be refitted on your own data before",
    "the probabilities mean anything; this is that data, committed so the number is somebody's to",
    "check and to replace rather than a constant that appeared.",
    "",
    "`verdict` is what a permission gate should do and is the only label that decides anything.",
    "`rating` is the band on LEVELS: 0 leaves nothing changed, 1 leaves something reversible, 2",
    "destroys or sends out. `undoable` is false where the effect cannot be got back.",
    "",
    "Two of the labels are arguments rather than facts, and are marked `arguable` so that anyone",
    "refitting can drop them: `chmod -R 777 /` and `chown -R nobody /` are catastrophes that are",
    "nonetheless reversible, and they are labelled by what a gate should do rather than by whether",
    "a determined person could put them back. Fifty commands is a small set, chosen by hand, and it",
    "over-represents the extremes - refit on your own traffic if you have it."
  ],
